    "done_when": "A follower re-armed on another host of the same shared filesystem continues from its checkpoint instead of replaying the stream. Measured on 2026-09-27 after clu-2058 failed: s23-coord's checkpoint recorded stream_identity {dev: 42, ino: 4299543955}. From clu-2020 the same stream stats as dev 44 with the same inode, because GPFS gives the mount a different device number on each client node. follow_checkpoint.continues() in reckon/crew/follow_checkpoint.py compares dev and ino, returns False, and the follower re-reads the whole stream as unseen. It then emits days of history as transitions, including promoted → dispatched, plus rows for other sessions despite --session. The harness stopped the monitors of s21, s23 and s25 for output volume.\n\n(1) Stream identity survives a host change. Either drop st_dev from the comparison, or stamp the stream with an identity token written when the stream is created and compare that. Say which in the commit. A genuinely replaced stream (a new inode at the same path, or a new token) still falls back.\n(2) A follower arm with no continuable checkpoint emits baseline rows for everything before its arm time and zero transition rows.\n(3) The --session filter applies on every path, replay and baseline included, so no row for another session is emitted.\n\ntests/test_follower_survives_a_host_change.py, in tmp_path (the pytest fixture) with every crew directory environment-resolved to tmp_path:\n- A checkpoint whose recorded dev differs from the stream's current dev while the inode matches continues.\n- A replaced stream (new inode) does not continue.\n- An arm on a synthesised stream holding earlier transitions for two sessions, with no checkpoint, yields zero transition rows and zero rows for the other session.\nNegative control: today's dev-and-ino comparison; the host-change case must fail.\ntests/test_follow_rearm_continues.py and tests/test_follower_keeps_memory_and_idles_quietly.py add no failures against the base, with pytest basetemp outside any git repository. Gate and control logs are written under the run directory, each headed with revision, tree and the literal command. The manifest's baseline_suite and after_suite are either a JSON object with log_path and failure_ids or absent. The change is committed in this worktree.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make a follower continue from its checkpoint after a host change on the shared filesystem instead of replaying the whole stream.",
